kull and bones  their location  they are at the virtual epicenter  geographical epicenter of the yale  campus  um  yale  as a school i've never gone to yale  i went to a neighboring college  um  yale has always been a school that  primarily  has produced  businessmen and lawyers  these businessmen and lawyers go into  not just small businesses but big  businesses  and into government  um  it's that kind of school it is basically  a masonic type of school  uh has a masonic type of emphasis  it has had a masonic type of emphasis  this  organization seems to be a  very much a masonic type of organization  is anything  wrong with that  i mean  they're  they give a  certain emphasis to the college  they set the tone  for the college  uh they have other organizations here  but  this particular group seems to um  be at the epicenter in more ways than  one  uh  is that so terrible  okay the question i think is whether  skull and bones is is a bad thing uh  whether it's so terrible that they have  all of these rituals  um  i think i'll just say i find it  intriguing skull and bones  engages in rituals that have been the  same rituals since 1832 that's partly  how  they lure their their members how they  get them to  to stay with the society and participate  in these sometimes strange rituals  throughout the year because the members  know that this is something that george  bush did this is something that william  howard taft did this is something that's  been done every year in this  organization since 1832.  does that reflect yale yes it does skull  and bones is really the the epitome of  yale  yale likes to live in the past in fact  yale has instead of  fixing broken windows instead of  replacing them it's sort of it likes to  patch them sometimes so they look old  and in the early 1900s  when yale was renovating the campus it  shows a particularly weathered quarry  from which to construct its buildings so  the campus would look older than it is  yale like skull and bones 